      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8875034::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "At strain rates of 10^2–10^4 s^-1, moderate-SFE HEAs exhibit concurrent partial-dislocation glide and mechanical twinning.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Concurrent partial-dislocation glide and twinning create dense fault and twin networks.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::016::discussion",
        "PMC7012927::web::005::in_situ_tem_straining_tests"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dense twin networks act as substantial barriers to dislocation motion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::016::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Twin networks or twin-boundary interfaces provide additional pathways for dislocation-mediated plastic deformation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::016::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fault and twin networks enhance dynamic strain hardening.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::016::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moderate-SFE alloys have a better dynamic strength-ductility balance than both substantially lower- and higher-SFE alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial-dislocation activity in moderate-SFE alloys progressively forms twin boundaries under dynamic stress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting twin boundaries impede further dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::016::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Activation of multiple slip systems prevents brittle failure and preserves ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moderate-SFE compositions produce 15–25% higher dynamic flow stress than lower- or higher-SFE baselines.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moderate-SFE compositions retain greater ductility, higher hardening rates, and greater energy absorption before failure at strain rates above 10^2 s^-1.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated Cr content produces significantly higher stacking-fault energy.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher stacking-fault energy favors dislocation motion relative to mechanical twinning.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8875034::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-SFE baseline alloys exhibit lower strain hardening because they form fewer twins.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8875034::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Very low-SFE alloys twin rapidly but undergo earlier strain localization instead of balanced work hardening.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism holds in single-phase FCC HEAs from −100 to 25 °C at strain rates of 10^2–10^4 s^-1.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
